<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/049G">Construction <span data-tag="049G">8.1.7.2</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category. We let $\operatorname{Cospan}^{\mathrm{all}, \mathrm{iso} }(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ denote the simplicial subset of $\operatorname{Cospan}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ whose $n$-simplices are diagrams </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =40pt@C=20pt{ X_{0,0} \ar [dr] &amp;  &amp;  X_{1,1} \ar [dr] \ar [dl]_{\sim } &amp;  \cdots &amp;  X_{n-1,n-1} \ar [dr] \ar [dl]_{\sim } &amp;  &amp;  X_{n,n} \ar [dl]_{\sim } \\ &amp;  \cdots \ar [dr] &amp;  &amp;  \cdots \ar [dr] \ar [dl]_{\sim } &amp;  &amp;  \cdots \ar [dl]_{\sim } &amp;  \\ &amp;  &amp;  X_{0,n-1} \ar [dr] &amp;  &amp;  X_{1,n} \ar [dl]_{\sim } &amp;  &amp;  \\ &amp;  &amp;  &amp;  X_{0,n}, &amp;  &amp;  &amp;  \\ } \]
</div>
<p> where each of the leftward-directed arrows is an isomorphism in $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. </p>
</article>
